{"text": "Category E is Visual Impairment. The educational description is: A student whose limited visual acuity or field substantially interferes with everyday participation, learning, and achievement unless presentation methods, materials, or the learning environment are adapted. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Aaliyah Johnson, who is in Grade 5 and uses she/her pronouns. Aaliyah has low vision related to ocular albinism. She reads enlarged digital text and uses a monocular for distance viewing; cognition and academic learning are age appropriate. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Aaliyah, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Aaliyah’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-E-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1125, "end": 0.675, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "E", "start": 0.6875, "end": 1.1, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.1125, "end": 1.3125, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Visual", "start": 1.325, "end": 1.7375, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 20}, {"text": "Impairment", "start": 1.75, "end": 2.5125, "start_char": 21, "end_char": 31}, {"text": "The", "start": 2.875, "end": 3.0625, "start_char": 33, "end_char": 36}, {"text": "educational", "start": 3.075, "end": 3.675, "start_char": 37, "